<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Winds hit Kansas, Oklahoma.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Winds hit Kansas, Oklahoma.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong winds were blowing through central Kansas and Oklahoma on Friday, grain merchandisers in the High Plains said.</p>
<p>Wind gusts in central Kansas were as high as 40 miles an hour, a dealer there said.</p>
<p>&quot;They say it's supposed to blow like this all day and into tomorrow,&quot; the dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged, although there was some firmness at mill locations in eastern Kansas.</p>
